(x_{11}x_{22} - x_{12}x_{21})^2.\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,{∇}_{X}f(X) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{11}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2} & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{12}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{21}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2} & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{22}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot {x}_{22} & 2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot (-{x}_{21}) \\\\ 2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot (-{x}_{12}) & 2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot {x}_{11}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{22} & -{x}_{21} \\\\ -{x}_{12} & {x}_{11}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2det(X)[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{22} & -{x}_{21} \\\\ -{x}_{12} & {x}_{11}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ![](images/79/790980ee64747a4ef3becd801431083d66839972cb271207807c43c53cf166fa.svg) we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{X}f(X) & =2(-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10-(-4)\\cdot \\frac{3}{2})[\\begin{aligned}10 & 4 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2(-5-(-6))[\\begin{aligned}10 & 4 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}20 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535861 17592186045417 true] [17592186203866 1071 "Consider the function $L: \\mathbb{R}^{2 \\times 3}   \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ defined by $L(\\mathbf{A}) = \\dfrac{1}{2}(\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b})^T(\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b}),$ where\n![](images/51/518bfea30c779d3e9dc1ab6b77b0ddaa9b938b56b0bb3b9e68d6c9b9cdae5666.svg)\nWhat is $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{A}} L$ at \n![](images/a1/a1e2b39a295cebfd8425e8ab73e4d915233ca3afbd4141c54332c38f1091be15.svg)" 13194139535861 17592186045417 true] [17592186203866 